      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[16]_{7}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $[a]_{7}=[b]_{7}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[16]_{7}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $17$ modulo $7.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[16]_{7} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\cdot 7+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\cdot 0+2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)} \\\\  & =[2]_{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
